flowchart TD
  prop["Proposed item"]
  pane["Worklist pane"]
  auth["Authorization record"]
  claim["Execution claim"]
  guard["bram-guard"]
  edits["Agent edits"]
  applied["Applied item"]
  route["Commit route"]
  commit["Git commit"]
  done["Pruned, kept in history"]

  prop -->|"shown on the board"| pane
  pane -->|"Start records approval"| auth
  auth -->|"starts claim"| claim
  prop -->|"coverage read by guard"| guard
  guard -->|"allow or deny"| edits
  claim -->|"boundary trees"| edits
  edits -->|"agent calls advance"| applied
  applied -->|"Commit click"| route
  auth -->|"checked by mutate and commit"| route
  route -->|"stages and commits"| commit
  commit -->|"prune and snapshot"| done
  pane -->|"Drop"| done

%% tip: Proposed item :: An entry in resources/worklist.json plus before/after prose in resources/worklist-drafts/<id>.md. Writing it is asking, not approval.
%% tip: Worklist pane :: The board where the user ticks items and clicks Start, Start & commit, Commit or Drop.
%% tip: Authorization record :: resources/.worklist-authorization.json: one slot, replaced by the next gate click, 30 minute TTL.
%% tip: Execution claim :: resources/.inflight-claim.json: which items are being worked on during a turn. Ends with the turn.
%% tip: bram-guard :: The Rust guard binary run as a PreToolUse hook (Claude, Codex, Antigravity) or plugin call (OpenCode). Fails closed on guard faults.
%% tip: Agent edits :: Edit, Write and shell writes by the agent, checked per call.
%% tip: Applied item :: status applied: changes on disk, awaiting commit approval. A begun proposed item can be committed too.
%% tip: Commit route :: worklist-commit: verifies approval, scope and message, then stages only the items' files or hunks.
%% tip: Git commit :: A path-scoped git commit, or a plumbing commit built from claim-interval patches when items share a file.
%% tip: Pruned, kept in history :: The row leaves worklist.json; the host snapshots each change under resources/worklist-history/.
%% tip: shown on the board :: Bram merges draft prose into the board payload so the pane sees one combined item.
%% tip: Start records approval :: The pane records the action through a Tauri command before the turn is sent.
%% tip: starts claim :: Recording an approval also writes the execution claim for those ids.
%% tip: coverage read by guard :: An edit is allowed when a proposed or applied item declares the path. Coverage is weaker than approval.
%% tip: allow or deny :: Exit code and stderr: the model reads the deny reason.
%% tip: boundary trees :: Each claim change captures a tree of the whole project, so changes can be attributed to intervals.
%% tip: agent calls advance :: The agent must call mutate op advance after applying. Nothing but the conventions makes it.
%% tip: Commit click :: Records a fresh approval; Start & commit skips the advance.
%% tip: checked by mutate and commit :: Routes check kind, ids and freshness against the stored record, not the button label.
%% tip: stages and commits :: Path-scoped add and commit, or hunk-by-hunk when another item owns lines in the same file.
%% tip: prune and snapshot :: The commit route prunes through the mutate handler; history snapshots follow.
%% tip: Drop :: Removes the row, not the bytes on disk.
